A QPR of the ideal circuit β with the overhead Eq. (48) is constructed in two steps. First, one applies the decomposition
Eq. (50) to each CNOT of β and merges state preparation maps P|0i that appear in Oα0 (if any) with the single-qubit gates of β
following the CNOT. Now all CNOT gates are replaced by noisy gates from Ω. The rest of the circuit consists of single-qubit
gates Uβ ∈ Γ and state preparations P|+i . At the second step, each of these ideal operations is replaced by its QPR constructed
above. Note that each CNOT contributes γ 2 to the total overhead γβ , see Eq. (50). Each single-qubit gate Uβ ∈ Γ or a state
preparation P|+i contributes at most γ to the total overhead. This proves Eq. (48).

